{"phase": "request_done", "request_result": {"token_ids": [32, 3165, 95085, 1433, 318, 54, 939, 8, 24546, 9626, 12964, 539, 24123, 7499, 7189, 310, 14733, 5638, 1518, 58565, 9463, 13, 1368, 264, 1785, 34942, 11, 279, 12964, 1817, 41224, 279, 1433, 310, 10229, 10839, 13726, 11, 311, 19413, 6501, 836, 4203, 318, 61413, 8, 310, 5790, 37285, 11, 1345, 19484, 1142, 632, 94085, 5981, 13, 271, 89494, 286, 1503, 524, 8032, 279, 1433, 1521, 424, 15756, 14973, 264, 12594, 4475, 1528, 11, 17191, 279, 7867, 314, 1433, 795, 421, 1902, 381, 45867, 2261, 12964, 13, 4213, 11, 424, 4021, 14988, 279, 39604, 314, 13726, 10839, 1238, 279, 28336, 26, 279, 1433, 8198, 279, 62411, 2450, 364, 1782, 3110, 4203, 13, 271, 2381, 3010, 11, 413, 264, 5883, 8059, 40161, 506, 220, 16, 15, 25, 15, 15, 6556, 321, 264, 28336, 13273, 506, 220, 16, 15, 25, 15, 20, 6556, 11, 264, 9626, 506, 220, 16, 15, 25, 16, 15, 6556, 7225, 279, 1433, 310, 11774, 279, 8059, 725, 37285, 11, 430, 279, 28336, 4026, 942, 424, 13, 271, 23201, 11, 37285, 321, 29310, 513, 12103, 10270, 887, 5706, 13, 19525, 2803, 34475, 421, 10839, 795, 79476, 1785, 26946, 11, 19248, 29310, 24546, 421, 32907, 13726, 635, 524, 38556, 440, 1754, 975, 725, 27510, 5134, 11, 19720, 19214, 27224, 2261, 10993, 13, 248046], "text": "A write-ahead log (WAL) ensures crash recovery by forcing transaction records to stable storage before acknowledging completion. If a system crashes, the recovery process scans the log to identify committed transactions, re-applying their changes (redo) to ensure durability, while rolling back uncommitted ones.\n\nCheckpointing does not replace the log because it merely marks a consistent database state, reducing the volume of log data that must be scanned during recovery. However, it cannot guarantee the persistence of transactions committed after the checkpoint; the log remains the authoritative source for those recent changes.\n\nFor example, if a bank transfer commits at 10:00 AM and a checkpoint occurs at 10:05 AM, a crash at 10:10 AM requires the log to prove the transfer\u2019s durability, as the checkpoint predates it.\n\nFinally, durability and isolation are distinct ACID properties. Durability guarantees that committed data survives system failures, whereas isolation ensures that concurrent transactions do not interfere with each other\u2019s intermediate states, maintaining logical consistency during execution.", "wall_seconds": 47.37502391694579, "first_token_seconds": 15.649057499947958, "wall_tokens_per_second": 4.517148115326932, "native_generation_tps": null, "prompt_tokens": 1536, "finish_reason": "stop", "accepted_drafts": 0, "verification_rounds": 0, "teacher_forwards": 0, "id": "explanation-1536-native-r0", "case_id": "explanation-1536", "method": "native", "warmup": false, "max_tokens": 256, "repeat": 8, "sample_repeat": 0, "eval_group_size": 32, "prompt_sha256": "9fb5d6cc5804d4eb3b980e7834308f7d643a7f8bb3f362142824d0431d6f59e4", "prompt_token_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 760, 2614, 26388, 14246, 17593, 369, 3870, 1132, 13, 21134, 279, 41559, 1238, 424, 26, 635, 524, 59987, 466, 2880, 279, 17593, 13, 198, 27, 15547, 29, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 15, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 15, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 16, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 16, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 17, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 17, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 18, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 18, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 19, 25, 264, 1152